<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-18494] Near cache not created with getCache</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-18494</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;The problem:&lt;br/&gt;
On affinity nodes everything works.&lt;br/&gt;
On client nodes and non-affinity nodes (i.e. filtered by some node filter) &amp;#8211; near configuration ignored when starting cache on demand from descriptor.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;-------&lt;br/&gt;
_The documentation (&lt;a href=&quot;https://ignite.apache.org/docs/latest/configuring-caches/near-cache#configuring-near-cache&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://ignite.apache.org/docs/latest/configuring-caches/near-cache#configuring-near-cache&lt;/a&gt;) says:&lt;br/&gt;
&quot;Once configured in this way, the near cache is created on any node that requests data from the underlying cache, including both server nodes and client nodes.&quot;&lt;br/&gt;
We expect the Near cache to be created for the cache proxy obtained with getCache, and getOrCreateNearCache does not need to be called because the NearConfiguration was initialized when the cache was created.&lt;br/&gt;
Reproducers show that this is not so.&lt;br/&gt;
Java reproducer &lt;span class=&quot;nobr&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/attachment/13054484/13054484_Issue.java&quot; title=&quot;Issue.java attached to IGNITE-18494&quot;&gt;Issue.java&lt;sup&gt;&lt;img class=&quot;rendericon&quot; src=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/images/icons/link_attachment_7.gif&quot; height=&quot;7&quot; width=&quot;7&quot; align=&quot;absmiddle&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; border=&quot;0&quot;/&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; without platformcache._&lt;/p&gt;</description>
